[Music]  hello  today we'll be talking about how to make  your data in a bucket public to  everyone on the internet this means that  your data will be readable to everyone  on the internet  i've created a bucket called tiny homes  in this bucket i'll be storing photos of  tiny homes  as you can see right now all the images  are private  but i want to make these images public  so people can access them  so the first step is to open the cloud  storage browser  in google cloud console when we are in  the bucket  we can see all the files that live in  the bucket  so to make a single file public what we  want to do is we want to click  the actions menu which is the three  little bars  to the side of the file  we want to select edit permissions from  the drop down menu  then we want to add a new entity the  entity name should be public  then all users and then reader and then  just click save  and as you can see we have a link that  we can share with anyone who wants to  view  this specific file in the bucket but  let's say we want to make all the images  in this folder public  it would be tedious to do the actions  that we performed earlier to every item  in the bucket so what we can do is we  can click the edit permissions button  add a new member called all users  set their role as storage object viewer  in the cloud storage section  and that's it we've made every image in  our bucket public  you

